From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:32:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: keep txqs scheduled while a reset or off-channel
 time skips them

mt76_txq_schedule_list() skipped a txq whose phy was resetting or off
channel without returning it to mac80211. ieee80211_next_txq() had
already taken it off the active list, and mac80211 only schedules it
again when a new frame is queued for it or when a dequeue meets a
stopped queue, which never happens here since nothing is dequeued.

So frames already queued for a station when an L1 or full reset began
(mt7915_mac_restart() schedules all txqs with MT76_RESET set; the L1
path sets it before disabling the tx worker), or while the phy was
scanning off channel, waited for the next frame of the same TID: up to
TCP's retransmit timeout, or for good for the last packets of a flow.

Return the txq before skipping it. ieee80211_next_txq()'s schedule
round keeps the same pass from seeing it again.

The skips for a missing wcid or one now on the other hw are left as
they are: those stations are being removed.

No unit test: this path needs mac80211's own txqs, which the fakes
don't provide (as for 0067).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tx.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tx.c b/tx.c
index 4b57b07b..ed962397 100644
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -649,8 +649,17 @@ mt76_txq_schedule_list(struct mt76_phy *phy, enum mt76_txq_id qid)
 		if (phy->hw != hw)
 			continue;
 
-		if (test_bit(MT76_RESET, &phy->state) || phy->offchannel)
+		/*
+		 * ieee80211_next_txq() took the txq off the active list, and
+		 * mac80211 only puts it back when a new frame is queued for it
+		 * (or a dequeue hit a stopped queue). Return it, or what's
+		 * queued now waits for the next frame after the reset or the
+		 * off-channel time, which may never come.
+		 */
+		if (test_bit(MT76_RESET, &phy->state) || phy->offchannel) {
+			ieee80211_return_txq(phy->hw, txq, false);
 			continue;
+		}
 
 		q = phy->q_tx[qid];
 
